  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The U.S. Consumer business is seeing softening demand and lower volumes as consumer sentiment weakens amid macroeconomic uncertainty. This top-line pressure is being partially offset by a sharply improved gross margin profile, driven by operational and supply chain efficiencies—including benefits from a foreign trade zone—that are lifting profitability per unit even as total revenue contracts.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management highlighted the margin-driven profit improvement that more than compensated for the sales decline, and demonstrated confidence through a fourth consecutive annual dividend increase. The focus on cost management and operational discipline has doubled operating profit, but the market’s negative reaction to the revenue shortfall suggests concern over the durability of demand recovery, leaving a mixed narrative of strong internal execution against a weak external backdrop.",
